{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened","id":969630,"title":"Can other Great Apes become Awakened?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T20:32:32-07:00","id":969630,"title":"Can other Great Apes become Awakened?","content":"I was watching The Flash, and it features Grodd as a psychic Gorilla, its kind of scary to see what something we treated as lesser than us turning into something greater than us. <br /> <br /> So with most settings that make humans special or attribute mystical powers to humans, I wonder why not Bonobos or Orangutans? Why not Chimpanzees or Gorillas? Humans are apes. It causes me to wonder how that factors into a setting where Awakened lived in a non-history as spiritually superior beings. Are apes just shells of a fallen world and the evolved humans was the best spot for our mystical souls? Or is being Awakened not necessarily dependent on a particular species?<br /> <br /> Can other Great Apes become Awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:36:42-07:00","id":969631,"title":"","content":"The Temenos, the collective soul of humanity, is separated from the Anima Mundi by the Omphalos, the Astral representation of language. So, no, great apes could not Awaken, because they don't have language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:31:18-07:00","id":969645,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin is correct but, since that'd end the thread, I'll play Devil's Advocate: Great Apes, like everything in the universe, have some manner of soul that is represented in the Astral. Deep within the Astral is the Wellspring; a symbol of the source of knowledge and uplift. If a creature drinks from it and endures its ravages, it may develop sufficient wisdom to command the divine symbols of the Heavens and Awaken. Such a creature, though, would be difficult to distinguish from a human with a gorilla body in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:46:04-07:00","id":969650,"title":"","content":"If Silver Age comics have taught me anything, adding gorillas to something automatically makes it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:55:23-07:00","id":969655,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of an Asimov story where a scientist uses an experimental drug to give a pig super intelligence, which the pig then uses to ensure it has all of the things a pig would want because it is still a pig, not a man.<br /> \u200bSo if someone created a Grodd type ape (Life with the help of Mind could do it, even make it a hereditary trait) what would the big beast want? Would curiosity drive it to seek out Mysteries with a capital 'M', or would its ambitions be limited to claiming dominance over a territory and a harem of females to give it offspring?<br /> The differences are what would make such an Awakened creature interesting (while the similarities would make it frightening).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:05:24-07:00","id":969662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969645#post969645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin is correct but, since that'd end the thread, I'll play Devil's Advocate</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, to play Devil's Advocate with myself: a lot of great apes can learn sign language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:12:21-07:00","id":969665,"title":"","content":"Indeed. And not simply learn sign language but it creatively, demonstrating empathy and theory of mind. Washoe, a signing chimpanzee, has demonstrated a capacity to understand the role of a recipient in communication; slowing her signing when communicating with new zoo keepers to make it easier for them to understand. Likewise, she's used the sign for tear to convey sympathy and sadness, despite crying not being something chimpanzees are physically capable of doing. That suggests empathy and an understanding of relational language, if not outright symbolism.<br /> <br /> Most interesting of all, gorillas typically fail the mirror test - a common test of cognitive capacity to recognize oneself as separate from one's environment - but Koko, the famed signing gorilla, passed it.<br /> <br /> And that's all without going into the more esoteric stuff, like the suggestions that chimpanzees develop religious behaviour towards large bodies of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:41:16-07:00","id":969675,"title":"","content":"If language is the only thing that separates non-human animals from Awakening, a strong case is probably with the more chatty of the cephalopod animals.<br /> <br /> Of course, from the very human-centric attempts to define language, one of the key factors in what makes human communication &quot;language&quot; is the features beyond communication. A good example is the ability to creatively construct new words for arbitrary reasons. For example, making up a new word just to fit a rhyming scheme in a poem. We have never observed such behaviors in any other animals; even other apes we've taught to speak a mutually intelligible communication system.<br /> <br /> That also fits in with Mage fairly well. The first instance of an Imago of a spell is very much an extension of that same concept: the ability to creatively apply parts of symbols into a unique expression that did not exist before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:46:49-07:00","id":969678,"title":"","content":"Hey, if there's ever a ChroD/Eclipse Phase crossover...<br /> <br /> Infinite Macabre needs uplifted gorilla mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:57:34-07:00","id":969685,"title":"","content":"something something Harambe is a Moros something something Mystery Play","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:27:39-07:00","id":969697,"title":"","content":"I hadn't considered the Astral or its relationship with Language. It sounds like from what others in the thread mentioned that the jury is still out on the potential for language among the great apes. <br /> <br /> More of what I am aiming at is that in the Mage setting, there is a really weird mystery. Mages claim we live in a fallen world, but humans evolved from other primates. So if Humans existed in a time before time (did they?), whats up with the other primates? How did evolution happen? Are Apes just part of the lie? Or is our failure to attribute personhood to them part of the lie? Is there sympathetic magical connections with apes because of this?<br /> <br /> Even deeper, as suggested by Geckopirateship, what about things that gain the ability to speak language that are alive? There are a lot of factions that could give apes language skills. I mean, its probably possible in our reality, so with magic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","user":"AForgeForThoughts","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:32:06-07:00","id":969699,"title":"","content":"It's only a matter of time until an African Gray Parrot has an Awakening, I think. Look up the story of Alex and be amazed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:35:31-07:00","id":969701,"title":"","content":"Yeah actually there are other candidates as well. As there are other species which approach our cognitive faculties. Awakened parrots or dolphins would be give even stranger implications to what Awakening was and what Mages from the Time Before would be like.<br /> <br /> I focused mainly on apes for the genetic similarities between us and them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:15:12-07:00","id":969718,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm wrong, but does not Supernal Magic streaming from <b><i>soul</i></b>? And true souls have only <i>humanity</i>, as other animals have spirits in Shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:22:29-07:00","id":969721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969718#post969718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm wrong, but does not Supernal Magic streaming from <b><i>soul</i></b>? And true souls have only <i>humanity</i>, as other animals have spirits in Shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;Humans don't have spirits&quot; issue makes it even weirder. I am not sure if that humans lacking spirits is caused by them having souls though. Humans may lack spirits because they are so complex that they cause multiple kinds of spirits to arise, no one spirits complicated enough to capture humans altogether. Maybe Father Wolf cursed them. Its another huge mystery. <br /> <br /> Also, the fact that humans don't have spirits doesn't need to apply to other animals that somehow had souls. An ape could have a soul and still create Ape spirits in the shadow. Which is interesting because this may lend an idea of what kinds of magic apes would be good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:24:49-07:00","id":969750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969697#post969697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages claim we live in a fallen world, but humans evolved from other primates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they in the CofD? Evolution in the CofD doesn't have to be as strong a theory as it is in reality. There's also nothing to say humans were not created from primates rather than evolved from them while evolution largely played out as science says it does. It is a supernatural setting after all, so lots of options exist for how humans came to be, and how that might have influenced why we're &quot;special&quot; in all the various ways the games make humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Apes just part of the lie? </div> </div> </div>Try not to confuse being part of the Fallen World with being part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> The Fallen World is the state of reality outside the Supernal. The Lie is the force that hides the Truth of the Supernal from the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Apes are part of the Fallen World, and also part of the Supernal World, they're not inherently part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are a lot of factions that could give apes language skills. I mean, its probably possible in our reality, so with magic... </div> </div> </div>But just like we can teach apes to communicate without teaching them the full extent of language despite trying, an ape that was magically enhanced wouldn't inherently have the full capacity that humans have in the setting regarding magical potential. Using magic to create an ape Sleepwalker, or even an ape Proximus might be possible sure, but considering mages can't get other humans to Awaken in any consistent or reliable way, there's really no way to do that to something mages give a human intellect to either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:05:18-07:00","id":970134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969750#post969750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they in the CofD? Evolution in the CofD doesn't have to be as strong a theory as it is in reality. There's also nothing to say humans were not created from primates rather than evolved from them while evolution largely played out as science says it does. It is a supernatural setting after all, so lots of options exist for how humans came to be, and how that might have influenced why we're &quot;special&quot; in all the various ways the games make humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that is possible. The setting isn't strongly defined, so I guess intelligent design or other weirder theories could be possible. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969750#post969750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try not to confuse being part of the Fallen World with being part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> The Fallen World is the state of reality outside the Supernal. The Lie is the force that hides the Truth of the Supernal from the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Apes are part of the Fallen World, and also part of the Supernal World, they're not inherently part of the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969750#post969750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just like we can teach apes to communicate without teaching them the full extent of language despite trying, an ape that was magically enhanced wouldn't inherently have the full capacity that humans have in the setting regarding magical potential. Using magic to create an ape Sleepwalker, or even an ape Proximus might be possible sure, but considering mages can't get other humans to Awaken in any consistent or reliable way, there's really no way to do that to something mages give a human intellect to either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually ape Sleepwalkers and Proximus are really cool though. I my idea was that you wouldn't directly create an Ape awakened, you would make a population of apes that had magically enhanced intelligence, which continue to exist for several generations. The idea is that one of them would eventually awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:10:32-07:00","id":970142,"title":"","content":"Since only humans experience Quiessence you could make the argument that all animals, including apes, are Sleepwalkers by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:13:22-07:00","id":970146,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the lie begins to infect them once they gain human-like cognitive faculties. Even worse something like this may really capture the attention of either the Abyss or the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:15:05-07:00","id":970150,"title":"","content":"The answer to that would depend entirely on the story you want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:41:45-07:00","id":970172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969718#post969718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm wrong, but does not Supernal Magic streaming from <b><i>soul</i></b>? And true souls have only <i>humanity</i>, as other animals have spirits in Shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>This and the language issue are connected. Not only are humans the only things with souls, they're the only things with a connection to the Temenos. If a chimpanzee could gain full capacity for language, could you say with absolute certainty that it would not gain a soul? Likewise, it's related to the humans not having spirits issue. If humans did not have language, if the Temenos was not separated from the Anima Mundi by the Omphalos, can you say with absolute certainty that humans would not have spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:48:07-07:00","id":970179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969697#post969697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages claim we live in a fallen world, but humans evolved from other primates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did humans evolved from other primates or is that simply part of the Lie and the origins of the world, life and man something that is currently considered mythological the Truth?<br /> <br /> Just saying your premise is based on understanding originating from within a world that is a Lie (since the game universe is a mirror of ours, and we'd all be Sleepers in game terms)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970172#post970172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a chimpanzee could gain full capacity for language, could you say with absolute certainty that it would not gain a soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only one way to find out, -cracks knuckles- bring in the Mind Master with Initiate Death and a chimpanzee! [unethical experiments ensue].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:50:01-07:00","id":970180,"title":"","content":"So I think this thread's basis assumes much that's worth remembering. For one, we haven't had a common ancestor with other great apes for about six million years. And our closest relatives, chimpanzees and bonobos, actually show quite a few behaviors and things not quite like with us, such as their recognition of reflections inherently and as far as I can gather they don't learn sign language like gorillas can. <br /> <br /> Just because we're related to other apes doesn't really inheently mean every feature is the same. This is shown as is, as we're well, pretty different the set of five fo us. And while no particular aspect of human cognition or langauge is unique to us, there's quite a bit in the specific combination we have that's unique to us and our extinct relatives. Humans, for instance, are the only animal who purposefully controls fire if I remember right. We're also probably the best (not unique, just best) at things like episodic and long term memroy. And while a theory of self is not unique to humans, it seems we have it on a scale not really seen in other animals.<br /> <br /> So while an interesting question, I think the matter of it is that probably not. Since apes aren't sapient in the same ways that we are, do not have the evolutionary history we do beyond a point where a significant amount has changed and don't demonstrate save in some superficial manners more than some of the very basic aspects of human intelligence, stuff that we wouldn't expect of them. In the case of the CofD, they simply don't have true souls to access the same parts of the Supernal as humans do. And it's probably tied into something rather unique to us that occurred in the alst few million if not few thousand years.<br /> <br /> For all we know, humanity was not able to do magic of any sort until the first person created art or something similar seventy thousand years ago in Africa. Or whatever history was like before the Fall. <br /> <br /> The premise is also simply built on bad logic. <br /> <br /> P1) All humans are apes.<br /> P2) All gorillas are apes.<br /> P3) Some humans can Awaken.<br /> P4) Because P1 and P3, some apes can Awaken.<br /> C) Because P2 and P4, gorillas can Awaken.<br /> <br /> This is false, mind. I don't have the time to show the Aristotelian syllogism gone awry, but basically it has some undistributed middle stuff going on about. And I think the relevant thing to remember is that just because humans and other apes are well, apes, doesn't mean that being an ape is an important part to being Awakened.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:57:41-07:00","id":970188,"title":"","content":"Seems like giving apes or, really, anything, a language would be something a cabal of life and mind-focused mages could do. Maybe with Fate or Time to help.<br /> <br /> Just some breeding until you get some massive purple apes and you can have Grape Ape the Hanna-Barberacanthus.<br /> <br /> Though I think any mage who would try to introduce a new species that was capable of Awakening would probably find themselves and their work brutally erased from history. And I wouldn't be so quick to point a finger at the Seers. It would undermine a lot of the Silver Ladder and Free Council.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> I think anything would fit with the right qualifications, but people like apes and it would take more work to get hornets to start talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:20:51-07:00","id":970269,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Omphalos doesn't separate <i>individual human souls</i> from the Anima Mundi. It separates <i>the entire Temenos</i>, the collective soul of the species. So, it may not be enough to teach a chimpanzee sign language. It may require an evolutionary step forward on the species scale, a new species of ape that shares humanity's capacity for the kind of nuanced grasp of language that is apparently just beyond chimpanzees and gorillas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As Nofather points out, such a thing would probably be within the power of an enterprising cabal, with the help of some Life, Mind, and Fate magic. Maybe some Time to speed up the process and some Death to check if it worked. But the implications, if it did work, would have absolutely tremendous and there are probably many powerful mages that would be invested in impeding their progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-15-2016, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:48:17-07:00","id":970283,"title":"","content":"I think if you got apes to the point where they could develop a Temenos they would develop one that's separate from humanity. Though, there'd be sideways access where human and ape ideas share overlap. I kind of doubt it's within the capability of Mages though, archmasters on the other hand, they do experiments like that with enough frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:59:08-07:00","id":970388,"title":"","content":"If it's just a matter of language, crows have developed language to the point of having differing dialects. They also manage an intelligence closer to our own than even apes. I'd put them at closer to Awakening, personally.<br /> <br /> But I still wouldn't have anything Awaken but humans, as only humans have a soul naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:11:00-07:00","id":970396,"title":"","content":"I don't have very much interest in Mage: The Awakening, but I'm totally down for a game if I can play a Gorilla Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:29:24-07:00","id":970411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970388#post970388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's just a matter of language, crows have developed language to the point of having differing dialects. They also manage an intelligence closer to our own than even apes. I'd put them at closer to Awakening, personally.<br /> <br /> But I still wouldn't have anything Awaken but humans, as only humans have a soul naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's why the Corvidae show up as familiars in so much literature, they already have one foot in the supernal door so to speak <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:41:45-07:00","id":970418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970388#post970388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's just a matter of language, crows have developed language to the point of having differing dialects. They also manage an intelligence closer to our own than even apes. I'd put them at closer to Awakening, personally.<br /> <br /> But I still wouldn't have anything Awaken but humans, as only humans have a soul naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, these things appear to be related. Humans are the only things with souls. Humans are the only things with a connection to the Temenos. The Temenos is separated from the Anima Mundi - the collective soul of everything else - by language. I don't know what Mage's standard for language is, but apparently Crows don't meet it because they don't have a Temenos. Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:55:07-07:00","id":970428,"title":"","content":"Correlation != causation and all that.<br /> <br /> Is there any indication that you cannot visit the Oneiros of someone with the Soulless condition? I couldn't find anything, though it's very easily possible that I just missed it. Given that souls are more or less interchangeable, I came to the conclusion that they're entirely unrelated to the Oneiros. Otherwise they wouldn't be interchangeable, given that the Oneiros is filled with things unique to the owner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:23:23-07:00","id":970474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970180#post970180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise is also simply built on bad logic.<br /> <br /> P1) All humans are apes.<br /> P2) All gorillas are apes.<br /> P3) Some humans can Awaken.<br /> P4) Because P1 and P3, some apes can Awaken.<br /> C) Because P2 and P4, gorillas can Awaken.<br /> <br /> This is false, mind. I don't have the time to show the Aristotelian syllogism gone awry, but basically it has some undistributed middle stuff going on about. And I think the relevant thing to remember is that just because humans and other apes are well, apes, doesn't mean that being an ape is an important part to being Awakened.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold your horses. I am not employing deductive logic. <br /> <br /> To be clear, I am not trying to prove anything or make a logical case for anything. I was not attempting to deduce the existence of non-human mages from what is stated in the books. I apologize if it seemed like I was attempting to make the case that there <b>must</b> be Ape mages <b>because </b>human apes can become mages. As we have seen in pretty much ever speculative thread on this forum, the authors get to decide what is absolutely true based off the themes, and everything else is spooky vagueness. This isn't a &quot;fan theory&quot; that I hope DaveB is going to come in and confirm for me. <br /> <br /> The only thing I am trying to get out of this thread is to explore a potential chronicle spanning mystery on the relationship between Humans as animals, Mages as Humans, and other animals. I thought an Ape Mage or Proximus would be a really really weird and could be a good central draw for a chronicle. This thread has so far been pretty productive because people had brought up various aspects of why a non human ape shouldn't be a Mage. So putting one in my own setting makes it an even stranger mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:58:47-07:00","id":970484,"title":"","content":"You might go another way. I've been reading sci-fi lately and in a book by Neal Asher the search for other intelligences on Earth was given up after fairly extensive research among the apes and dolphins. However years later someone happened to leave, I forget what exactly, but some sort of a internet-accessing virtual reality suit on when they weren't using it and a hornet flew into it and started communicating across the internet. It was revealed that hornets existed as a hive mind. This led to new searches for intelligence among similar creatures but wasps were to hornets as apes are to us. The hornets were accepted as a species and when sometimes people succumb to that atavistic fear of insects and kills a hornet, they can be leveraged into a form of indentured servitude where they're tasked with exploring and experiencing things a swarm of hornets cannot.<br /> <br /> I'm newish to Mage and my knowledge of the Astral is confined to scraps of memories at best. I don't know how the Temenos is required for Awakening, but I seem to recall that while werewolves were unable to access the Temenos, they were able to access some other Astral world. And they had souls in that edition as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:40:51-07:00","id":970505,"title":"","content":"You could work it in either version of Transgression, though, since there's a Merit that lets you play as a Mane and intelligent gorillas are enough of a scifi staple that there are probably a ton of intelligent gorilla Manes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:07:31-07:00","id":970521,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, Werewolves don't actually take part in the Temnos, when they dream or astral project, they skip the Temnos and go all the way to the Anima Mundi without any of the previous steps a mage needs to travel there. They also don't begin being flayed apart when they go into the Anima Mundi. (This could be wrong, I haven't read Astral Realms in a while).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:35:51-07:00","id":970552,"title":"","content":"A few random facts:<br /> <br /> 1) The Omphalos protects the collective thoughts and dreams of humanity by isolating them as a &quot;Temenos&quot;. Omphalos is also an artificial construct.<br /> <br /> 2) When you &quot;lose soul&quot;, you lose, among other things, your capability to connect with other people.<br /> <br /> 3) There is a big ass spire growing from Omphalos up to the Anima Mundi, symbolizing mankind's connection to the Dreamtime and was supposedly used as a scaffolding for the Celestial Ladder.<br /> <br /> 4) Well, it grew once. Now it's being reabsorbed by typhonides of the Aeon of Death, supposedly by the order of &quot;gods&quot;. Typhonides would devour Temenos as well, but can't because of Omphalos.<br /> <br /> 5) There is a new connection to the Dreamtime, known as the Swath, established on July 16, 1945. It becomes more pronounced as time goes on, and there are rumors about a realm existing in it, that symbolizes the fixing of Swath's diseased nature and essentially perfecting humans' connection to the Dreamtime.<br /> <br /> 6) Spires called the Watchtowers grow, too, out of the Supernal Realms on the other side of reality, though unlike the neolithic mages, most modern Awakened probably don't notice it. It's also relatively less stressful for mages to sign the Towers today.<br /> <br /> <br /> Make of it what you will.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> As for &quot;losing souls&quot;, I would say that their connection to Temenos and Omphalos is essential for today's humans' normal perception of life. There was a time when Omphalos didn't exist, with all the resulting consequences.<br /> <br /> There is also a place in the Dreamtime called The Wellspring, where animals, supposedly including humans, can gain sapience and even Awaken, without needing Temenos. Or Omphalos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-16-2016, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:03:49-07:00","id":970561,"title":"","content":"The thing about the Spire being part of the Ladder is pure conjecture, I'm not sure how widespread that theory is.<br /> <br /> Where does the bit about the Wellspring come from? I'm not sure I've ever heard about it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:05:52-07:00","id":970562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970561#post970561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the Spire being part of the Ladder is pure conjecture, I'm not sure how widespread that theory is.<br /> <br /> Where does the bit about the Wellspring come from? I'm not sure I've ever heard about it before.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said &quot;supposedly&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Wellspring, it's from the <i>Astral Realms</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:08:05-07:00","id":970564,"title":"","content":"i figured that's what you were saying, just wanted to make sure we were on the same page.<br /> <br /> And thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:21:43-07:00","id":970566,"title":"","content":"There's a brief mention in Astral Realms of the possibility of an Awakened Elephant. It's just a hook, mentioned alongside the Wellspring.<br /> <br /> I would rule any animal that has taken a drink from the Wellspring can theoretically Awaken, but I probably wouldn't bring them in as anything more than an anomaly. Though if a player wanted to play one and had cool ideas surrounding it, I wouldn't stand in their way.<br /> <br /> Great apes are just like any other animal in this matter, to me. Though I do have to wonder what is considered Human as far as usual Awakenings are concerned, such as Neanderthals and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:43:23-07:00","id":970573,"title":"","content":"I have this theory. In 1E there were hints about the early awakened followed dragons into atlantis and about crystal dragon bones. So I've came up with this:<br /> <br /> It's a cycle, at one point of time there is only one species that has the capacity to Awaken and serve as a conduct between the phenomenal and the supernal. After a time the whole species ascends and at that moment another species inherits the potential towards awakening. However the Fall propably broke that cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:21:06-07:00","id":970582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970573#post970573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this theory. In 1E there were hints about the early awakened followed dragons into atlantis and about crystal dragon bones. So I've came up with this:<br /> <br /> It's a cycle, at one point of time there is only one species that has the capacity to Awaken and serve as a conduct between the phenomenal and the supernal. After a time the whole species ascends and at that moment another species inherits the potential towards awakening. However the Fall propably broke that cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are insinuating that before we have inteligent reptilians sorcerers rulers of Earth!? All conspiracy theories were right - Reptilians ARE ruling reality as Ascendent Masters! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/instances/500x/56040097.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:58:05-07:00","id":970598,"title":"","content":"Just in case it was too vague, my previous post insinuated that the Ladder is being slowly rebuilt, this time the right way, with Swath and the Watchtowers &quot;growing&quot; toward each other. Oracles can be sneaky like that.<br /> <br /> If so, the Exarchs are fucked and probably don't even realize it yet.<br /> <br /> The Diamond Wheel is always in motion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-16-2016, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:33:30-07:00","id":970835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970598#post970598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swath and the Watchtowers &quot;growing&quot; toward each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just my English level being not high enough, but is not Swath just some large pool of goo of chemicals, not proper Spire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:40:31-07:00","id":970837,"title":"","content":"Just because it's not a spire doesn't mean it isn't a connection between the Temenos and the Anima Mundi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:02:42-07:00","id":970957,"title":"","content":"You know, I think the most important thing to note here is that<br /> <br /> A. Mages have considered this question<br /> B. Mages have most likely made multiple attempts at creating hyperintelligent gorillas <br /> <br /> Meaning that in Mage's setting, it's probably been done multiple times. Whether that means there are actual gorilla mages running around, or it all went abyssal-shaped, is what you have to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:05:47-07:00","id":970958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970552#post970552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few random facts:<br /> <br /> There is a new connection to the Dreamtime, known as the Swath, established on July 16, 1945. It becomes more pronounced as time goes on, and there are rumors about a realm existing in it, that symbolizes the fixing of Swath's diseased nature and essentially perfecting humans' connection to the Dreamtime.<br /> Make of it what you will..</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://Atom bomb successfully tested - Jul 16, 1945 - HISTORY.com\" target=\"_blank\">The first Nuclear testing </a>is an ominous thing to hang the future of humanity upon as it relates to the primordial cosmos. Since it is growing, seems like it's a count down to for an apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:57:31-07:00","id":971188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=969650#post969650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Silver Age comics have taught me anything, adding gorillas to something automatically makes it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's just like bacon? Awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}